1
00:00:06,883 --> 00:00:10,469
Henry Ford was born on 30 July 1863,

2
00:00:10,469 --> 00:00:13,012
on a farm near Dearborn, Michigan.

3
00:00:13,429 --> 00:00:15,911
He wrote that he disliked farm work,

4
00:00:15,911 --> 00:00:18,051
and that his toys were tools.

5
00:00:18,165 --> 00:00:21,789
By about fifteen, he could repair almost any watch.

6
00:00:22,073 --> 00:00:25,151
In 1896 he finished the Quadricycle,

7
00:00:25,151 --> 00:00:27,079
a gasoline-powered vehicle.

8
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:34,133
Ford Motor Company followed, incorporated on 16 June 1903 with $28,000 in capital.

9
00:00:34,133 --> 00:00:37,243
In 1908 Ford introduced the Model T,

10
00:00:37,243 --> 00:00:40,789
priced at about $825: a car, he recalled,

11
00:00:40,789 --> 00:00:42,575
for the great multitude.

12
00:00:42,859 --> 00:00:46,255
At Highland Park, which opened in 1910,

13
00:00:46,255 --> 00:00:50,221
the moving assembly line came in stages in 1913.

14
00:00:50,335 --> 00:00:54,713
Building one Model T chassis once took roughly 12.5 hours.

15
00:00:54,827 --> 00:00:58,325
By early 1914, about 93 minutes.

16
00:00:59,343 --> 00:01:03,557
In 1914 Ford announced $5 for an eight-hour day,

17
00:01:03,557 --> 00:01:06,331
in place of about $2.34 for nine.

18
00:01:06,445 --> 00:01:10,011
To earn all of it, workers faced home inspections.

19
00:01:10,125 --> 00:01:13,965
Historians still debate whether that was reform or control.

20
00:01:13,965 --> 00:01:18,273
In 1917 Ford began the River Rouge complex in Dearborn,

21
00:01:18,273 --> 00:01:22,953
finished in 1928: steel, power and assembly on one site,

22
00:01:22,953 --> 00:01:26,111
employing up to about 100,000 people.

23
00:01:26,225 --> 00:01:33,327
On 7 March 1932, police and Ford guards fired on unemployed marchers heading for the plant,

24
00:01:33,327 --> 00:01:34,997
killing four that day.

25
00:01:35,111 --> 00:01:41,727
On 26 May 1937, Ford’s Service Department men beat union organizers at an overpass,

26
00:01:41,727 --> 00:01:43,539
including Walter Reuther.

27
00:01:43,653 --> 00:01:47,145
On 20 June 1941, after a walkout,

28
00:01:47,145 --> 00:01:50,673
Ford, the last major Detroit automaker to hold out,

29
00:01:50,673 --> 00:01:52,343
signed with the union.

30
00:01:52,627 --> 00:01:59,329
By his own account, Ford’s factories worked almost entirely for the government in the First World War.

31
00:01:59,329 --> 00:02:04,679
In 1942, at Willow Run, Ford began building B-24 Liberator bombers;

32
00:02:04,679 --> 00:02:08,525
by 1944, one left the line about every hour.

33
00:02:08,942 --> 00:02:13,330
The plant held about 3.5 million square feet under one roof,

34
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:16,505
and employment peaked at about 42,000.

35
00:02:16,788 --> 00:02:19,444
Workers were scarce and housing short:

36
00:02:19,444 --> 00:02:24,103
one month the plant hired 2,900 people and lost 3,100.

37
00:02:24,216 --> 00:02:27,465
Wartime need brought many women into the plant.

38
00:02:29,248 --> 00:02:34,170
On 22 May 1920, The Dearborn Independent began a series,

39
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:35,809
“The International Jew.”

40
00:02:35,922 --> 00:02:37,953
It ran for 91 weeks.

41
00:02:38,236 --> 00:02:41,452
It drew on The Protocols of the Elders of Zion,

42
00:02:41,452 --> 00:02:44,046
a forgery, and blamed Jews for wars,

43
00:02:44,046 --> 00:02:46,123
finance and cultural decline.

44
00:02:46,236 --> 00:02:47,907
Jews were its targets.

45
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:52,109
The articles became a book, translated into many languages.

46
00:02:52,392 --> 00:02:55,998
In 1924 it attacked the lawyer Aaron Sapiro,

47
00:02:55,998 --> 00:02:57,495
who sued for libel.

48
00:02:57,608 --> 00:03:02,511
On 30 June 1927, Ford issued a retraction and apology.

49
00:03:02,624 --> 00:03:05,396
Historians still ask how involved he was,

50
00:03:05,396 --> 00:03:07,215
and whether he meant it.

51
00:03:07,498 --> 00:03:10,778
Henry Ford died on 7 April 1947,

52
00:03:10,778 --> 00:03:14,669
aged 83, at Fair Lane, his estate in Dearborn.

53
00:03:14,952 --> 00:03:19,795
The Model T stayed the best-selling car in history until 1972.

54
00:03:20,078 --> 00:03:27,269
Historians still disagree on how to weigh his engineering and wages against his antisemitism and labor record.
